# 1. Introduction

## 1.1 Purpose of this Document
This comprehensive user manual serves as the primary instructional guide for operating the Voucher Posting & Authorization System. It is purposefully designed to assist all designated stakeholders—including Makers, Checkers, Approvers, and Administrators across various operational teams (such as SBI GLIF, TCS GLIF, and TCS IMPL)—in navigating the application accurately and efficiently. The document outlines the end-to-end processes required for configuring Voucher IDs (VIDs), initiating manual or bulk financial postings, and executing multi-tiered authorization workflows. By providing clear, step-by-step instructions alongside strict business rules, this manual ensures that users can perform their daily financial operations securely and in full compliance with standard Maker-Checker protocols. Whether you are submitting a new financial batch, auditing a pending request, or tracking a voucher's entire lifecycle, this guide will serve as your complete reference to the system's capabilities.

## 1.2 System Overview & Key Features
The Voucher Posting & Authorization System is a secure, role-based financial application built to manage, validate, and route general ledger postings. It minimizes human error through strict system-level validations and ensures transparency through an immutable audit trail.

**Key Features Include:**
*   **Strict Maker-Checker Separation:** Enforces that no single user can both create and approve a financial entry, guaranteeing a secure separation of duties.
*   **Dynamic Voucher IDs (VIDs):** Utilizes pre-configured blueprints (created by SBI GLIF) that act as templates, ensuring Makers only post transactions to approved categories.
*   **Dual Entry Methods:** Supports intuitive Manual Data Entry for ad-hoc requests and robust Bulk Excel Uploads for processing thousands of rows simultaneously.
*   **Real-Time Mathematical Validation:** The system actively intercepts errors by forcing exact Debit and Credit balancing across all Branch and Currency combinations before a batch can even be submitted.
*   **Flexible Execution Scheduling:** Allows Final Approvers to post vouchers immediately or schedule them to automatically execute at a specific time later in the day.
*   **Comprehensive Audit Trails:** Features a detailed "View & Action" dashboard that tracks every stage, action, timestamp, and user remark throughout the voucher's lifespan.
*   **End-of-Day (EOD) Protections:** Automatically detects active banking EOD processes and safely disables new voucher entries until the cycle completes.

## 1.4 The Voucher Lifecycle: A High-Level Flow

The journey of a voucher from initial setup to final database execution follows a strict, sequential pipeline. Below is a high-level representation of this lifecycle:

```text
 ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │                 STAGE 1: CONFIGURATION                 │
 │  SBI GLIF Team creates a new Voucher ID (VID), sets    │
 │  the description, and assigns it to a target role.     │
 └──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
                            │
                            ▼
 ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │                  STAGE 2: INITIATION                   │
 │  Maker (TCS GLIF / IMPL) selects the VID and submits   │
 │  data via Manual Entry or Bulk Excel Upload.           │
 └──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
                            │
                            ▼
 ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │                 STAGE 3: VERIFICATION                  │
 │  Checker reviews the batch, verifies the data/Excel    │
 │  file, and Approves or Rejects the request.            │
 └──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
                            │
                            ▼
 ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │                 STAGE 4: FINAL APPROVAL                │
 │  Final Approver (SBI GLIF) does the ultimate review,   │
 │  approves the batch, and defines the Execution Time.   │
 └──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
                            │
                            ▼
 ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │                  STAGE 5: EXECUTION                    │
 │  System executes the batch into the core ledger either │
 │  Immediately or at the Scheduled Time.                 │
 └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
